# §7.102: config/ ships with the bundle — the runtime config lives there.
#
# BUT the real config must NOT ship: config/edge.json holds the plaintext
# secrets (deepseek / dashscope / tavily / bocha / edge api keys).
#
# Note the mechanism, because it is easy to get wrong: npm pack honours
# .npmignore INSTEAD of .gitignore whenever .npmignore exists. The
# `config/edge.json` rule in .gitignore therefore has NO effect on the
# published tarball — before this rule was added, `npm pack` shipped the
# real key file and the Makefile's `make package` copied it into the
# release tarball as well.
#
# What ships instead: config/edge.example.json (the tracked template) and
# config/privacy-policy.json. A deployment that needs real values creates
# config/edge.json from the template, or lets install.sh place one at
# ~/.dsh-edge-agent/edge.json (edge-config.ts lookup candidate #2).
config/edge.json
